1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.
Matthew 11:28 (KJV)

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:25,000
The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want. He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.
Psalm 23:1-2 (KJV)

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.
Isaiah 26:3 (KJV)

4
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:25,000
Be still, and know that I am God.
Psalm 46:10 (KJV)

5
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:25,000
Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.
John 14:27 (KJV)

6
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:25,000
I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.
Psalm 4:8 (KJV)

7
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:25,000
But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.
Isaiah 40:31 (KJV)

8
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:25,000
Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him cometh my salvation.
Psalm 62:1 (KJV)

9
01:13:00,000 --> 01:13:25,000
And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.
Philippians 4:7 (KJV)

10
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:25,000
Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.
1 Peter 5:7 (KJV)

11
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:25,000
Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.
Matthew 11:29 (KJV)

12
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:25,000
He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name's sake.
Psalm 23:3 (KJV)

13
01:49:00,000 --> 01:49:25,000
He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.
Psalm 91:1 (KJV)

14
01:58:00,000 --> 01:58:25,000
And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.
Exodus 33:14 (KJV)

15
02:07:00,000 --> 02:07:25,000
Jesus stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.
John 7:37 (KJV)

16
02:16:00,000 --> 02:16:25,000
Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him.
Psalm 37:7 (KJV)

17
02:25:00,000 --> 02:25:25,000
In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength.
Isaiah 30:15 (KJV)

18
02:34:00,000 --> 02:34:25,000
Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the LORD hath dealt bountifully with thee.
Psalm 116:7 (KJV)

19
02:43:00,000 --> 02:43:25,000
The eternal God is thy refuge, and underneath are the everlasting arms.
Deuteronomy 33:27 (KJV)

20
02:52:00,000 --> 02:52:25,000
The LORD will give strength unto his people; the LORD will bless his people with peace.
Psalm 29:11 (KJV)

